📅 Day 13 – Constructors, Object Lifecycle & Inheritance

Full Stack Web Development with Java Internship

Today’s session focused on understanding Constructors, Object Lifecycle, and Inheritance in Java. These concepts are fundamental to Object-Oriented Programming (OOP).

🔹 Topics Covered
1️⃣ Constructors in Java

A constructor is a special method used to initialize objects.

Key points discussed:

Constructor name must be same as class name

Constructors do not have a return type

Automatically called when object is created

Used to initialize instance variables

Types of Constructors:

Default Constructor → No parameters

Parameterized Constructor → Accepts parameters

Constructor Overloading → Multiple constructors with different parameter lists

🔹 2️⃣ Object Lifecycle

The mentor explained the complete lifecycle of an object:

Object creation using new keyword

Memory allocation in the heap

Constructor execution

Object usage

Garbage collection when object is no longer referenced

Understood how Java manages memory automatically using Garbage Collector.

🔹 3️⃣ Inheritance

Inheritance allows one class to acquire properties and methods of another class.

Key concepts covered:

Use of extends keyword

Parent class (Super class)

Child class (Sub class)

Code reusability

Method overriding (introduction)

Inheritance helps in building hierarchical relationships and promotes reuse of code.

